WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
Long ago, a rabbi compared
this whole world to a hallway.

2
00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.850
Beyond it lies a banquet
hall: the world to come.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:11.410
His advice was simple:
prepare in the hallway.

4
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.570
Yet the Torah itself says almost
nothing about life after death.

5
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.510
Its rewards are long
life, family and the land.

6
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.350
So what do Jews believe follows death?

7
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.550
In this mission, you'll meet the ideas
Jews have developed over the centuries,

8
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.950
from Sheol to the world to come.

9
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.880
Then you'll compare what Orthodox
and Reform Jews believe today,

10
00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.140
and weigh up how much it matters.

11
00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:38.920
Your mission: find out what
Jews believe follows death.
